{"type":"thinking","text":"Let me understand GTFS semantics and the bug.\n\nGTFS: service date; trips with times >= 24:00:00 belong to service date but run next civil day. Query at Saturday 00:00 for 30 min should include:\n- R7 service FRI 2025-07-04 clock 24:12:00 -> departure 2025-07-05T00:12:00Z (Friday late-night bus). Should appear.\n- X3 service EXTRA exception active 2025-07-05 clock 00:19:00 -> departure 2025-07-05T00:19:00Z. Should appear.\n- S1 service SAT 2025-07-05 is inactive due exception -> should NOT appear.\n- E2 East not stop River.\n\nCurrent deployed board expands only query's civil date, so it computes for date=2025-07-05, only SAT and EXTRA, gets X3 only. Misses R7.\n\nPrevious version presumably \"all early morning trips moved to previous day\" — bug where it only looks at previous service date for times < 04:00, thereby missing X3 (a Saturday EXTRA at 00:19). We need fix to consider both the query's civil date service expansion and the previous service date's 24+ hour trips, with exceptions resolved against the service date. Preserve both types.\n\nNeed design robust query over a time window up to 3 hours, potentially crossing multiple service dates? Window left-closed right-open max 3h. Need enumerate candidate service dates whose trip departures might fall in [from, from+minutes*60000). Since clocks can go to 47:59:59, a trip on service date D can depart as late as D+1 23:59:59 (clock 47:59:59). So for query at civil date Q, candidates service dates include Q and Q-1, possibly Q-2? A clock 47:59:59 on service date Q-2 = Q at 23:59:59, so could fall in query window if query starts on Q. But max window 3h means if query at Q 00:00, Q-2 47:59:59 = Q-1? Wait 47:59:59 = 24:00 + 23:59:59, i.e., next day at 23:59:59. Service date Q-2 + 47:59:59 = (Q-2 + 2 days) 23:59:59 = Q 23:59:59. For query on Q at 23:30 window 30 min, yes Q-2 trip could be included. So candidate service dates whose date + clock fraction lies in window. Since max clock 47:59:59, departure for service date D ranges [D 00:00:00, D+2 00:00:00). So for query window [from, to) with to <= from+3h, candidate service dates D such that D <= to and D+2 > from. That is D in dates from floor(from)-2? Let's reason: departure = D + offset where offset in [0, 2 days). To intersect [from,to), need D < to (if offset >=0, D <= departure < to) and D > from - 2 days (since departure < D+2 days, from < D+2days => D > from-2days). So D can be from from-2days up to to. In civildates: from date minus 2 days, minus 1, and from date, plus possibly next date if to extends past midnight. For max 3h windows: candidate dates from date(from)-2 through date(to) inclusive maybe. But easier: iterate service dates from floor(from) - 2 days to floor(to) inclusive (plus 1 for safety), each date, resolve calendar/exceptions for that service date, expand trips, compute actual departure, filter window. Need handle exceptions per service date.\n\nImportant semantics: calendar lists regular service dates per service. exceptions either add or cancel service on specified date. GTFS: If exception active=true, service added on date even if not in calendar (or just service runs). If active=false, service removed. The current code uses override?.active ?? calendar includes date. That's fine: exception active true => true; false => false; no override => calendar includes. Extras add active.\n\nNeed be careful: exceptions may exist for date but service not otherwise in calendar; active true means include.\n\nNeed candidate dates. Could derive from relevant feed trips and calendar? Simpler enumerate dates from date(from) - 2 days through date(to). Since clocks max 47:59:59, that's enough. But check if to can be exactly on next day+? If from=23:00 Q and window 3h => to=Q+1 02:00. Candidate from date Q-2, Q-1, Q, Q+1. Dates Q+1 trips with clock 00:xx depart Q+1 00:xx within window. Good. Need maybe date(to)+? If to = Q+1 02:00, a trip on service date Q+1 with clock 00:30 departs before to. Included because we include date(to) = Q+1. A trip on service date Q+1 with clock 00:00 = exactly Q+1 00:00 < to, included. If to exactly Q+1 00:00 (from Q 21:00), window [21:00, 00:00) excludes Q+1 00:00, including date(to)=Q+1 harmless after filtering. Could include one extra day. For safety iterate date(from)-2 through date(to)+1 maybe; filtering handles. But need not overcomplicate. Let's use from date -2 to date(to) inclusive. Actually departure for D=date(to) with clock 00:00: if date(to) date is to date, departure at date start <= to; if to exactly midnight, exclusive but filter. Good. D=date(to)+? cannot be < to except if to is later than its start; date(to)+1 start > to always, so no. So through date(to) inclusive suffices with offset >=0. For D = date(from)-2: departure min D start = from date -2 00:00, could be >? Still any departure on D could be as late as D+2 start. Intersect [from,to). If from is e.g Q 00:00, D=Q-2 max departure < Q 00:00, so excluded. Fine. Could D=date(from)-1 needed yes. date(from) yes. date(to) maybe next date if window crosses. So -2 to date(to). Actually consider from Q 23:00, window to Q+1 02:00, D=Q-1 with clock 47:59:59 = Q+1 23:59:59 not in window; D=Q-2 with clock 47:59:59 = Q 23:59:59 in window! So -2 covers. D=Q-3 max departure < Q 00:00 < from, no. Good.\n\nNeed parse dates and add days. Could use Date.UTC or Date.parse. Query start includes Z ISO. Need preserve milliseconds. Compute service date midnight using Date.parse(date+\"T00:00:00Z\") or Date.UTC. Date arithmetic robust for UTC no DST.\n\nNeed maybe validate input? Not necessarily. Interface same.\n\nPotential issue: Date.parse(start) accepted. date = new Date(from).toISOString().slice(0,10). That's UTC date suitable.\n\nImplement helper addDays maybe. Could use ms increments 86400000.\n\nCandidate service dates can be generated from midnight of from date - 2 days through midnight of to date inclusive. Need to get date of to: Date.parse(start)+minutes*60000. If minutes=0 window empty; maybe handle. to might be computed. For date(to), use new Date(to - 1?) If to exactly midnight from next day, including date(to) harmless. Could use new Date(to).toISOString().slice(0,10). Fine.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: serviceDate in result should be the service date, not civil date. For R7 serviceDate \"2025-07-04\", departure \"2025-07-05T00:12:00.000Z\". X3 serviceDate \"2025-07-05\", departure \"2025-07-05T00:19:00.000Z\". S1 canceled. Sorting by departure then tripId ASCII. localeCompare may not be ASCII lexicographic exactly? README says ASCII tripId ascending. localeCompare default locale can differ, e.g. case ordering maybe. Better use a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0 for ASCII based on JS string UTF-16; IDs likely ASCII. Departure ISO strings compare works because same format. Could sort by numeric time or ISO. Current use localeCompare. Requirement \"ASCII tripId\". Use direct relational comparison to ensure deterministic ASCII. But changing sort maybe okay. Could keep departure localeCompare since ISO. Better implement comparator using departure strings and tripId ASCII. Note duplicate same trip maybe different service dates? Could happen. No requirement.\n\nNeed tests reproducing complaint. The user says \"补能复现投诉的回归测试\" — add regression test that reproduces complaint. Should include test at Saturday 00:00 for River showing both R7 and X3 (and not S1) perhaps. Also test previous-regression: temporary extra not lost. Could explicitly assert:\n- departures(feed,\"River\",\"2025-07-05T00:00:00Z\",30) => [{tripId:\"R7\",serviceDate:\"2025-07-04\",departure:\"2025-07-05T00:12:00.000Z\"},{tripId:\"X3\",serviceDate:\"2025-07-05\",departure:\"2025-07-05T00:19:00.000Z\"}]\n- maybe assert S1 canceled not present. That one test reproduces both types? \"同时保留两类服务\" — add two tests possibly. Also maybe test window crossing midnight starting Friday before midnight includes R7 and Saturday? Example query Friday 23:50 to 00:20: includes R7 at 00:12 and X3 at 00:19. Could be a good test for crossing midnight. But original complaint is Saturday 00:00 refresh. We'll add robust tests:\n  1. regression for complaint: Saturday 00:00 refresh sees Friday R7 and Saturday EXTRA X3, not canceled SAT S","truncated":true}
